OL,3,ABritish Museum boss 'sorry' for Bayeux
OL,4,ATapestry visitor issues
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe head of the British Museum has
OL,7,Fapologised for the experience some
OL,8,Fvisitors have had at its blockbuster
OL,9,FBayeux Tapestry exhibition.
OL,11,FThe London institution has announced
OL,12,Fchanges to how visitors see the
OL,13,Fhistoric work over concerns of
OL,14,Fovercrowding.
OL,16,F"Anyone that doesn't have a good
OL,17,Fexperience, we're really sorry about
OL,18,Fthat and we want to put it right,"
OL,19,FNicholas Cullinan told the BBC's
OL,20,Fculture and media editor Katie Razzall.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/19
